WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.530
Every session starts with a choice.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.170
Your usual model, or a faster, cheaper one.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.980
Cheaper looks obvious.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.980
But a cheaper model can make more trips to finish the same job.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.400
Fast Decisions makes that call once, before the session starts.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.270
It checks the price.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.730
It checks the project.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.860
Then it prints its reasons.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.570
A project with more than three hundred files stays on your usual model.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.230
A prediction is not a bill.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.990
So you run both, on the same task, and compare.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.170
Your own matched runs answer that.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.820
Nothing here is a promise.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.840
Fast Decisions.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.520
Find the agent decisions worth making cheaper.
